The redistributed material is data/base_c7.json: the 367-word independent set
I_0 in C_7^(box 5), the auxiliary set X, the eight private pairs and the two
transversals.  It has been transcribed from Lean into JSON and the two
transversals have been named P^H and P^V to match the notation of the paper;
the underlying words are unchanged.

The 367-word independent set is originally due to Sven Polak and Alexander
Schrijver, "New lower bound on the Shannon capacity of C7 from circular
graphs", Information Processing Letters 143 (2019) 37-40.

The combining rules and terminal codes in shannon/bpz.py are likewise
transcribed from ShannonBounds/Substitutions.lean and
ShannonBounds/TerminalCodes.lean at the same commit.  Verbatim snapshots of
all three source files are included under upstream/ with SHA-256 pins, and
tests/test_upstream_pinned.py machine-checks the transcriptions against them.
